92
00:02:31,737 --> 00:02:33,637
Let's meet up with Celes and company.

93
00:02:33,637 --> 00:02:35,147
This is odd.

94
00:02:35,147 --> 00:02:37,017
Odd? What's wrong?

95
00:02:37,017 --> 00:02:38,137
Everything.

96
00:02:38,137 --> 00:02:42,997
From the moment we started this
 training camp, nothing's made any sense.

97
00:02:42,997 --> 00:02:43,987
I'm surprised.

98
00:02:44,857 --> 00:02:48,837
You're sharper than I thought you were.

99
00:02:48,837 --> 00:02:52,647
And here I thought all you have in your head
 are Machine Dragons and Lux.

100
00:02:53,557 --> 00:02:56,137
Yeah. Every now and then I can be prettyâ€”

101
00:02:56,137 --> 00:02:58,327
Hey! Don't make fun of me!

102
00:02:58,327 --> 00:03:00,457
Miss Lisha? Krulcifer?

103
00:03:01,027 --> 00:03:02,247
Airi?

104
00:03:02,247 --> 00:03:04,917
We took care of the Diablos.

105
00:03:04,917 --> 00:03:05,917
Are you all right?

106
00:03:06,327 --> 00:03:09,417
Yes. We managed to repel the attacks too.

107
00:03:09,417 --> 00:03:14,317
However, Shalice and Tillfur's Machine Dragons
 were damaged and they can't fight.

108
00:03:11,047 --> 00:03:13,167
This sucks...

109
00:03:13,167 --> 00:03:13,987
Yes.

110
00:03:13,987 --> 00:03:15,547
Don't give me "Yes"!

111
00:03:14,317 --> 00:03:17,687
Also, we found the entrance to the lowest level,

112
00:03:15,547 --> 00:03:16,637
Yes.

113
00:03:16,637 --> 00:03:18,427
Is that the only thing you can say?!

114
00:03:17,687 --> 00:03:23,427
but according to La Krulshe,
 the presence of some kind of key is required.

115
00:03:18,427 --> 00:03:19,007
Yes.

116
00:03:19,007 --> 00:03:21,647
Stop with the one word answers!

117
00:03:23,427 --> 00:03:25,137
What could that be?

118
00:03:27,167 --> 00:03:29,507
If you say that again,
 we'll start just saying "Oh, no!"

119
00:03:29,507 --> 00:03:31,427
Oh, good idea!

120
00:03:30,017 --> 00:03:31,427
Come on! Say it!

121
00:03:30,637 --> 00:03:34,567
We have no choice but to
 retreat for the time being.

122
00:03:32,257 --> 00:03:32,867
Yes.

123
00:03:32,867 --> 00:03:34,007
Oh, no!

124
00:03:34,007 --> 00:03:36,337
This is no time to be fooling around!

125
00:03:38,367 --> 00:03:40,527
What are you doing here?!

126
00:03:40,527 --> 00:03:41,907
Easy, there.

127
00:03:41,907 --> 00:03:45,017
If you kill me, that female dies too.

128
00:03:45,017 --> 00:03:46,167
What does that mean?

129
00:03:46,707 --> 00:03:50,147
She has one of these planted in her.

130
00:03:50,147 --> 00:03:53,127
One of the Ragnarok seeds I've been growing.

131
00:03:53,717 --> 00:03:54,837
What?!

132
00:03:55,307 --> 00:03:57,677
When you plant one into a living being,

133
00:03:57,677 --> 00:04:00,567
it eats them from the inside
 and turns them into an Abyss.

134
00:04:00,567 --> 00:04:06,307
Then they become a faithful servant of the Ragnarok, unable to defy its will.

135
00:04:06,797 --> 00:04:14,527
By the looks of it, this one has been defying the orders 
and suffering constant fever and headaches.

136
00:04:16,207 --> 00:04:17,137
Orders?

137
00:04:17,137 --> 00:04:20,087
I had the Ragnarok give that order.

138
00:04:20,087 --> 00:04:24,787
The order to kill you, Lux Arcadia!

139
00:04:28,937 --> 00:04:35,717
Defying the order means suffering a living hell,
 eventually turning to dust and dying.

140
00:04:38,047 --> 00:04:42,427
So how much longer do you plan on waving that thing in my face?

141
00:04:45,427 --> 00:04:47,737
Let's make a deal.

142
00:04:55,277 --> 00:04:59,737
<i>As things stand, the girl has only several days left to live.</i>

143
00:04:59,737 --> 00:05:00,957
What?

144
00:05:01,697 --> 00:05:03,527
So here's my offer.

145
00:05:03,527 --> 00:05:08,167
I'll use this to make the Ragnarok give an order to save the girl,

146
00:05:08,167 --> 00:05:11,667
and you open the door of the ruin floating outside for me.

147
00:05:12,257 --> 00:05:13,417
What door?

148
00:05:13,417 --> 00:05:17,657
A key is necessary to open the door to the lowest level.

149
00:05:17,657 --> 00:05:20,297
Use that key girl of yours.

150
00:05:21,757 --> 00:05:23,647
You have two days.

151
00:05:23,647 --> 00:05:25,417
Don't drag your feet.

152
00:05:25,417 --> 00:05:26,207
Wait!

153
00:05:26,207 --> 00:05:27,727
Who are you?!

154
00:05:28,437 --> 00:05:32,077
Were you wondering why I have the same hair color as you and your siblings?

155
00:05:32,817 --> 00:05:35,037
I'm the real deal.

156
00:05:35,037 --> 00:05:36,837
Unlike you lot.

157
00:05:39,867 --> 00:05:42,907
<i>What should I do?</i>

158
00:05:42,907 --> 00:05:43,987
Lu.

159
00:05:45,437 --> 00:05:47,057
Phi.

160
00:05:47,057 --> 00:05:49,377
I'm hungry.

161
00:05:54,847 --> 00:05:57,697
I see. You don't remember anything.

162
00:05:57,697 --> 00:06:00,387
Did I cause any problems?

163
00:06:00,387 --> 00:06:02,327
Not at all.

164
00:06:02,327 --> 00:06:03,217
How is it?

165
00:06:03,217 --> 00:06:04,017
Good.

166
00:06:06,227 --> 00:06:08,687
You too, Lu. Open wide.

167
00:06:09,757 --> 00:06:11,767
N-No. I'm not hungry.

168
00:06:11,767 --> 00:06:12,907
Open wide.

169
00:06:12,907 --> 00:06:14,177
I told you...

170
00:06:14,177 --> 00:06:15,357
Open wide.

171
00:06:15,357 --> 00:06:17,417
Okay, fine.

172
00:06:19,417 --> 00:06:20,877
What's wrong?

173
00:06:20,877 --> 00:06:23,657
Nothing. Don't worry about it.

174
00:06:32,277 --> 00:06:33,037
<i>What's wrong?</i>

175
00:06:38,297 --> 00:06:39,627
Why?!

176
00:06:39,627 --> 00:06:42,427
Philuffy was supposed to
 have been saved back then!

177
00:06:42,427 --> 00:06:43,557
Why?!

178
00:06:48,817 --> 00:06:50,847
I remembered.

179
00:06:51,477 --> 00:06:55,247
It hasn't been seven years since I last saw Philuffy.

180
00:06:55,247 --> 00:06:58,587
We met was five years ago, on this island.

181
00:06:58,587 --> 00:07:04,527
You rescued Philuffy when the former empire had kidnapped her for human experimentation.

182
00:07:04,527 --> 00:07:07,877
But Philuffy was already dead.

183
00:07:08,787 --> 00:07:11,477
What? No!

184
00:07:11,477 --> 00:07:13,617
That's not possible!

185
00:07:13,617 --> 00:07:15,537
She's alive right now!

186
00:07:15,537 --> 00:07:18,627
Yes. She woke up.

187
00:07:18,627 --> 00:07:22,757
She was much tougher and stronger than before.

188
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:29,227
It was when I because headmistress of this school
 that I found out Philuffy had turned into an Abyss.

189
00:07:29,227 --> 00:07:30,527
An Abyss?

190
00:07:30,527 --> 00:07:33,347
I have to go into the ruins.

191
00:07:33,347 --> 00:07:38,307
With the technology from them,
 I may be able to save Philuffy.

192
00:07:38,307 --> 00:07:40,697
Is that why you brought us to this island?

193
00:07:40,697 --> 00:07:43,107
She's running out of time.

194
00:07:43,107 --> 00:07:48,907
I must reach the lowest level and find a way to save her.

195
00:07:48,907 --> 00:07:51,727
Even if it means giving up my own life.

196
00:07:54,007 --> 00:07:55,237
Phi.

197
00:07:57,657 --> 00:07:58,877
Why?

198
00:07:59,837 --> 00:08:02,927
Why are you visiting my mother's grave?

199
00:08:03,987 --> 00:08:07,067
Just leave me alone.

200
00:08:08,137 --> 00:08:10,657
This is supposed to cheer you up.

201
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:14,267
My mother does it for me.

202
00:08:29,047 --> 00:08:30,407
Lux.

203
00:08:30,407 --> 00:08:32,677
Hey! Lux!

204
00:08:32,677 --> 00:08:33,497
Lux!

205
00:08:34,797 --> 00:08:36,707
He's finally awake.

206
00:08:36,707 --> 00:08:39,467
Quit daydreaming already!

207
00:08:39,467 --> 00:08:44,247
We've been tuning Bahamut for you 
all morning, you know!

208
00:08:44,247 --> 00:08:45,717
I-I'm sorry.

209
00:08:46,267 --> 00:08:49,787
So, are we done now?

210
00:08:49,787 --> 00:08:54,937
Yes. If I send you the release code,
 you can use the Over Limit.

211
00:08:54,937 --> 00:08:58,477
I'll go get permission to use it
 from the headmistress.

212
00:09:00,427 --> 00:09:03,607
Hopefully the day you'll need to use it never comes.

213
00:09:05,177 --> 00:09:07,407
It's been a while, Lux,

214
00:09:07,407 --> 00:09:11,017
the weakest hero, who sacrificed himself
 and suffered defeat for his ideals.

215
00:09:11,697 --> 00:09:13,117
That voice...

216
00:09:13,117 --> 00:09:14,407
Is that you?!

217
00:09:14,407 --> 00:09:16,177
Fugil Arcadia?!

218
00:09:16,177 --> 00:09:18,257
Where are you?!

219
00:09:18,257 --> 00:09:23,547
You know, I find the melody of the horn
 Hayes had quite displeasing.

220
00:09:23,547 --> 00:09:25,237
Don't you feel the same way?

221
00:09:25,927 --> 00:09:28,087
What do you know?

222
00:09:28,457 --> 00:09:30,647
If you want to save your childhood friend,

223
00:09:30,647 --> 00:09:35,057
the only way is to destroy the horn and
 defeat the Ragnarok controlling the seed.

224
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:40,397
Naturally, it's up to you whether you trust this information.

225
00:09:40,397 --> 00:09:43,777
By the way, I have a question for you.

226
00:09:50,617 --> 00:09:52,167
Phi!

227
00:09:52,167 --> 00:09:54,217
You have to stay in bed!

228
00:09:54,217 --> 00:09:56,457
I know.

229
00:09:56,917 --> 00:09:59,327
I know that there's an Abyss inside of me.

230
00:09:59,947 --> 00:10:00,877
Huh?

231
00:10:00,877 --> 00:10:04,117
But it's okay, I guess.

232
00:10:04,927 --> 00:10:10,757
After mom got sick and died,
 Relie was so sad and lonely.

233
00:10:10,757 --> 00:10:13,157
So I decided I can't afford to die.

234
00:10:13,797 --> 00:10:15,847
You're sad and lonely too.

235
00:10:16,757 --> 00:10:18,557
But it's okay now.

236
00:10:19,277 --> 00:10:22,377
Now you have many people
 who care about you.

237
00:10:22,377 --> 00:10:24,817
And Relie won't be lonely with you around.

238
00:10:24,817 --> 00:10:25,817
Phi...

239
00:10:25,817 --> 00:10:29,807
You've become strong,
 so it's all going to be okay.

240
00:10:29,807 --> 00:10:30,877
No!

241
00:10:32,647 --> 00:10:34,567
I can't do anything.

242
00:10:34,567 --> 00:10:36,367
I'm still weak.

243
00:10:38,377 --> 00:10:39,597
On that day...

244
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:42,197
Because you saved me...

245
00:10:42,197 --> 00:10:44,007
Because you've been there for me...

246
00:10:44,007 --> 00:10:46,567
I was able to fight.

247
00:10:46,567 --> 00:10:48,567
So don't leave me!

248
00:10:48,567 --> 00:10:53,057
I'll save you for real this time!

249
00:10:54,007 --> 00:10:55,637
I see.

250
00:10:55,637 --> 00:10:57,727
You haven't changed.

251
00:10:59,537 --> 00:11:00,767
Thank you.

252
00:11:01,467 --> 00:11:02,417
I'll wait for you.

253
00:11:11,997 --> 00:11:15,027
I'm happy to have you all back here so soon!

254
00:11:15,737 --> 00:11:20,747
What is the key we need to proceed?

255
00:11:20,747 --> 00:11:23,887
I'm sorry, but I cannot tell you that.

256
00:11:23,887 --> 00:11:25,157
I see.

257
00:11:25,157 --> 00:11:26,717
Very well, then.

258
00:11:26,717 --> 00:11:27,967
Everyone, stand back!

259
00:11:27,967 --> 00:11:30,627
I'll break the door with Seven Heads!

260
00:11:30,627 --> 00:11:31,227
What?!

261
00:11:31,227 --> 00:11:33,487
P-Please don't do that!

262
00:11:32,047 --> 00:11:33,487
Krulcifer.

263
00:11:33,487 --> 00:11:35,067
I understand.

264
00:11:35,067 --> 00:11:37,467
It's okay. Leave it to me.

265
00:11:46,327 --> 00:11:49,147
The door opened just like that!

266
00:11:49,147 --> 00:11:51,597
Krulcifer, who are you?

267
00:11:51,597 --> 00:11:57,787
I was the first one to meet La Krulshe,
 so I was simply recognized as her master.

268
00:11:58,317 --> 00:11:59,147
Right?

269
00:11:59,147 --> 00:12:00,227
Um...

270
00:12:00,227 --> 00:12:01,407
I see.

271
00:12:01,407 --> 00:12:03,677
Krulcifer is so refined.

272
00:12:03,677 --> 00:12:06,897
Unlike a certain princess who tries to solve everything with force.

273
00:12:08,087 --> 00:12:09,247
I see.

274
00:12:09,247 --> 00:12:12,097
Anyway, let's proceed ahead.

275
00:12:18,327 --> 00:12:20,597
So this is the lowest level.

276
00:12:20,597 --> 00:12:24,517
It doesn't look like the kind of place we'd find
 Machine Dragons or ancient documents.

277
00:12:24,957 --> 00:12:28,667
This <i>is</i> the right place, isn't it?

278
00:12:28,667 --> 00:12:30,567
This is the right place.

279
00:12:31,957 --> 00:12:35,567
I have successfully restored the memories I had lost.

280
00:12:35,567 --> 00:12:37,947
I remember everything.

281
00:12:37,947 --> 00:12:40,287
What I must do is...

282
00:12:40,287 --> 00:12:44,357
wipe out every single one of you.

283
00:12:45,337 --> 00:12:49,247
The clan that betrayed my masters,
 and everyone like them.

284
00:12:49,247 --> 00:12:50,497
La Krulshe!

285
00:12:50,497 --> 00:12:51,047
What are youâ€”

286
00:12:51,047 --> 00:12:53,077
Thank you, my prince!

287
00:12:55,047 --> 00:12:56,167
Hayes!

288
00:12:56,167 --> 00:13:01,317
You foolishly did exactly as planned.

289
00:13:01,317 --> 00:13:03,807
Thanks to you, I had no trouble getting in.

290
00:13:05,517 --> 00:13:06,827
Phi!

291
00:13:06,827 --> 00:13:08,307
Why is she here?!

292
00:13:08,307 --> 00:13:14,817
If I give a strong enough order, there will be
 no room for defiance. She has to obey.

293
00:13:14,817 --> 00:13:16,057
Fools!

294
00:13:21,107 --> 00:13:23,127
This is an order, monster girl!

295
00:13:23,127 --> 00:13:25,457
Kill them all!

296
00:13:30,397 --> 00:13:31,777
Bahamut!

297
00:13:35,647 --> 00:13:38,927
Airi, Headmistress, stay close to me.

298
00:13:38,927 --> 00:13:41,807
I won't allow you to raise a hand against my master!

299
00:13:45,367 --> 00:13:46,737
Unmanned Machine Dragons?!

300
00:13:51,147 --> 00:13:52,357
How are they so quick?!

301
00:13:52,877 --> 00:13:54,907
This isn't how a Wyvern normally moves.

302
00:13:54,907 --> 00:13:57,647
Could that be... Over Limit?!

303
00:13:58,107 --> 00:13:59,027
I'll pin her down!

304
00:14:06,407 --> 00:14:07,537
Celes!

305
00:14:08,047 --> 00:14:09,957
Why, you!

306
00:14:09,957 --> 00:14:11,587
Missing Fate.

307
00:14:14,507 --> 00:14:15,727
Wise Blood!

308
00:14:17,757 --> 00:14:18,757
My Divine Raiment!

309
00:14:19,547 --> 00:14:20,217
You're slow.

310
00:14:22,647 --> 00:14:23,847
Damn it!

311
00:14:26,647 --> 00:14:28,067
Be careful!

312
00:14:28,067 --> 00:14:32,207
Philuffy's Divine Raiment disables other Machine Dragons' Divine Raiments!

313
00:14:40,857 --> 00:14:43,037
All right, then.

314
00:14:45,357 --> 00:14:48,207
I see you're not moving
 in the shadows any more.

315
00:14:48,207 --> 00:14:49,287
What's it to you?

316
00:14:49,287 --> 00:14:51,247
Why did you come here?

317
00:14:51,247 --> 00:14:54,197
To bear witness to your majesty's exploits, my princess.

318
00:14:54,797 --> 00:14:58,477
You mean to bear witness to your brother's death.

319
00:15:03,897 --> 00:15:05,137
That sound!

320
00:15:05,537 --> 00:15:06,437
No!

321
00:15:13,517 --> 00:15:14,647
It is!

322
00:15:22,897 --> 00:15:29,267
The orders you give to Abysses and the Ragnarok
 through the horn fade after some time, don't they?

323
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:32,497
So you overrode my orders.

324
00:15:35,517 --> 00:15:36,597
Hayes!

325
00:15:37,797 --> 00:15:39,747
This is the end of the road for you.

326
00:15:39,747 --> 00:15:42,377
If you surrender, we shall spare your life.

327
00:15:42,847 --> 00:15:44,917
This is your final warning.

328
00:15:46,957 --> 00:15:49,407
My final warning?

329
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:51,347
It seems you are still unaware.

330
00:15:52,097 --> 00:15:55,857
You're the ones who fell for my trap!

331
00:15:58,387 --> 00:15:59,527
Is that what I think it is?!

332
00:16:03,997 --> 00:16:05,117
A Ragnarok!

333
00:16:05,787 --> 00:16:08,487
I brought along a new one,

334
00:16:08,487 --> 00:16:11,477
in order to take control of monster girl over there.

335
00:16:14,287 --> 00:16:16,787
Lisha! We're up against a Ragnarok.

336
00:16:16,787 --> 00:16:18,957
Let's all attack at once!

337
00:16:18,957 --> 00:16:20,797
Got it. Let's do this!

338
00:16:29,257 --> 00:16:31,317
Is that a Ragnarok?

339
00:16:31,317 --> 00:16:33,137
How disappointing.

340
00:16:33,137 --> 00:16:35,597
Wait! Something's not right.

341
00:16:36,747 --> 00:16:37,647
Everyone, dodge!

342
00:16:43,787 --> 00:16:47,607
The nice thing about this one is that its high-speed regeneration strengthens it.

343
00:16:47,607 --> 00:16:49,867
The more damage it receives,
 the stronger it gets.

344
00:16:51,697 --> 00:16:53,127
This is bad!

345
00:16:53,127 --> 00:16:55,237
At the rate we'll allâ€”

346
00:16:59,587 --> 00:17:02,887
Miss Lisha, allow me to use it.

347
00:17:02,887 --> 00:17:06,117
That other power hidden within Bahamut.

348
00:17:06,117 --> 00:17:08,107
You mean Over Limit?

349
00:17:08,107 --> 00:17:08,967
No!

350
00:17:08,967 --> 00:17:10,797
Using it is too dangerous!

351
00:17:10,797 --> 00:17:13,077
You're already at your breaking point.

352
00:17:13,077 --> 00:17:15,307
If you push yourself any further, you could...

353
00:17:15,307 --> 00:17:18,017
I can't let this end here!

354
00:17:18,017 --> 00:17:20,227
I don't want to have any more regrets!

355
00:17:20,977 --> 00:17:22,177
All right.

356
00:17:22,177 --> 00:17:25,487
I'll send you the release code from my Tiamat.

357
00:17:25,487 --> 00:17:27,337
Hold out for sixty seconds!

358
00:17:27,337 --> 00:17:28,067
Okay!

359
00:17:28,657 --> 00:17:31,157
Reload on Fire!

360
00:17:35,347 --> 00:17:38,377
<i>Make sure you come back to me, Lux!</i>

361
00:17:38,787 --> 00:17:43,337
I hope you've made your peace, my prince!

362
00:17:46,927 --> 00:17:48,507
<i>I have a question for you.</i>

363
00:17:49,757 --> 00:17:54,467
<i>Do you really want to save
 that childhood friend of yours?</i>

364
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:57,937
<i>Even if you do save her,
 nothing is going to change.</i>

365
00:17:58,467 --> 00:18:02,147
<i>You can't protect anything.
 You can't do anything.</i>

366
00:18:02,147 --> 00:18:05,607
<i>Your ideals are empty.</i>

367
00:18:05,607 --> 00:18:07,467
End Action!

368
00:18:17,197 --> 00:18:18,647
Fool!

369
00:18:18,647 --> 00:18:23,917
Did you forget that the Ragnarok becomes stronger with every hit you land?!

370
00:18:25,037 --> 00:18:26,757
<i>You haven't changed.</i>

371
00:18:26,757 --> 00:18:30,677
<i>You're just as foolish and weak
 as you were back then.</i>

372
00:18:30,677 --> 00:18:33,177
<i>And despite that, I...</i>

373
00:18:35,137 --> 00:18:36,177
Lux!

374
00:18:36,557 --> 00:18:39,847
It's over, you idiot prince playing the hero!

375
00:18:39,847 --> 00:18:42,807
Everyone who idolized you is going to die!

376
00:18:42,807 --> 00:18:45,107
The new kingdom will fall!

377
00:18:45,107 --> 00:18:47,557
And it's all your fault!

378
00:18:49,647 --> 00:18:50,777
No, it's not!

379
00:18:51,567 --> 00:18:57,037
You don't know anything about Lu,
 so don't talk to him like that!

380
00:18:57,037 --> 00:18:58,727
You!

381
00:18:58,727 --> 00:18:59,997
What do <i>you</i> know?!

382
00:19:00,477 --> 00:19:03,207
I know.

383
00:19:03,207 --> 00:19:08,087
Lu was always trying to change
 this kingdom, even if it hurt him.

384
00:19:08,087 --> 00:19:09,647
I know everything.

385
00:19:09,647 --> 00:19:11,087
Lux, can you hear me?!

386
00:19:11,087 --> 00:19:13,767
I sent you the instructions for
 releasing the Machine Dragon!

387
00:19:13,767 --> 00:19:15,887
Use the Over Limit!

388
00:19:17,357 --> 00:19:19,097
So fight!

389
00:19:19,097 --> 00:19:23,687
Not someone else's desires. For yourself, Lu!

390
00:19:24,297 --> 00:19:26,397
Thank you, Phi.

391
00:19:28,927 --> 00:19:31,697
Over Limit On!

392
00:19:40,997 --> 00:19:44,537
That's... Bahamut's true form.

393
00:19:44,957 --> 00:19:46,557
I-Impossible!

394
00:19:46,557 --> 00:19:48,507
Evade it, Ragnarok!

395
00:20:09,407 --> 00:20:10,607
How?!

396
00:20:10,607 --> 00:20:12,797
How could my Ragnarok lose?!

397
00:20:12,797 --> 00:20:15,467
We must retreat, Your Highness.

398
00:20:17,947 --> 00:20:20,957
I still have servants waiting nearby.

399
00:20:20,957 --> 00:20:21,627
I'll get him thisâ€”

400
00:20:21,627 --> 00:20:23,667
It's pointless, Hayes.

401
00:20:23,667 --> 00:20:27,527
You can't defeat him, because you don't even see what he's trying to achieve.

402
00:20:27,527 --> 00:20:28,167
What?!

403
00:20:28,607 --> 00:20:33,797
A Ragnarok that becomes ever stronger
 can't be defeated even with a Divine Raiment.

404
00:20:33,797 --> 00:20:40,187
That's why he intentionally made it stronger
 and used its own strength against it.

405
00:20:40,187 --> 00:20:44,597
Though it's a tactic made possible only by the Over Limit Bahamut.

406
00:20:46,357 --> 00:20:51,277
<i>You truly are my dreadful weakest enemy, Lux.</i>

407
00:21:01,657 --> 00:21:02,967
What in the world happened?!

408
00:21:02,967 --> 00:21:04,997
What have I been doing?!

409
00:21:05,707 --> 00:21:07,277
There's only one thing I can do!

410
00:21:07,277 --> 00:21:08,867
Good night.

411
00:21:13,457 --> 00:21:16,417
Um... aren't you sitting a bit too close?

412
00:21:16,417 --> 00:21:18,727
It's because I'm helping you get better.

413
00:21:18,727 --> 00:21:20,967
Does that really help?

414
00:21:25,997 --> 00:21:28,207
You seem to be feeling better.

415
00:21:28,207 --> 00:21:31,457
Yes. I'm fine as long as I don't strain myself.

416
00:21:31,457 --> 00:21:34,397
Getting used to the horn's sound
 helps me fight it.

417
00:21:34,397 --> 00:21:37,077
I see. Glad to hear it.

418
00:21:37,817 --> 00:21:39,737
Say, Lu...

419
00:21:40,367 --> 00:21:43,477
I'm okay now.

420
00:21:43,477 --> 00:21:46,077
Because you kept your promise.

421
00:21:47,597 --> 00:21:48,957
Thank you, Lu.

422
00:21:50,637 --> 00:21:51,957
I love you.

423
00:22:07,027 --> 00:22:12,097
